@startuml
' DG contribution I5: Ernest (ernestgoh-god).
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 150
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
hide footbox

participant ":CommandDispatcher" as Dispatcher #F1F5F9
participant ":FileStorage" as Storage #DBEAFE
participant ":PlanCodec" as Plans #DBEAFE
participant ":StateCodec" as Snapshots #DBEAFE
participant "Files\n(static API)" as Files #F1F5F9

note over Dispatcher, Storage
  Recurrence, allocation and output preparation already succeeded.
  Live state still refers to the previous snapshot/plan.
end note
Dispatcher -> Storage : savePlan(plan)
note over Storage, Plans : A PlanCodec is created for this call (constructor omitted).
Storage -> Plans : encode(plan)
Plans -> Snapshots : encodeForPlan(plan.source())
Snapshots --> Plans : full source text
Plans --> Storage : source + frozen-result text
Storage -> Storage : writeAtomically(text)

alt filesystem operations succeed
    Storage -> Files : createDirectories(parent)
    Storage -> Files : createTempFile(parent, ...)
    Files --> Storage : sibling temporaryFile
    Storage -> Files : writeString(temporaryFile, text, UTF_8)
    Storage -> Files : move(temporaryFile, file,\nATOMIC_MOVE, REPLACE_EXISTING)
    Files --> Storage : target replaced
    Storage --> Dispatcher : return
    ref over Dispatcher
      Publish saved source and plan.
      See command transactions for AppState calls.
    end ref
else preparation, writing or replacement throws
    ref over Storage, Files
      One filesystem operation above throws;
      subsequent operations are not attempted.
    end ref
    Files --> Storage : filesystem exception
    Storage -> Storage : create StorageException(cause)
    Storage -> Storage : removeTemporaryFile(temporaryFile, failure)
    opt temporary file was created
        Storage -> Files : deleteIfExists(temporaryFile)
        alt cleanup succeeds
            Files --> Storage : deleted / already absent
        else cleanup fails
            Files --> Storage : cleanup exception
            Storage -> Storage : failure.addSuppressed(cleanupException)
        end
    end
    Storage --> Dispatcher : throw StorageException
    note over Dispatcher : Keep previous live state; report rejection.
end

note over Storage, Files
  Encoding failures occur before filesystem changes.
  Atomic replacement requires provider support; no non-atomic fallback.
  This is not a power-loss durability guarantee.
end note
@enduml
